  "rationale": "The official provider player (provider-player) titles recording 56029 'Jun 01, 2007 Citizen Advisory Committee – Addison, TX' with a structured video index of community topics, establishing the convened body as a Citizen Advisory Committee. The Council document (citizen-council-june2007) independently corroborates that a real municipal 'Citizen Advisory Committee' existed in Addison and that the City Council was set to 'Discuss the Process for Receiving the Citizen Advisory Committee Recommendations' (Item #S6), proving the body is a genuine city body; however, that document is the Council's own work-session record and does not make this recording a City Council meeting or a joint meeting, so addison-tx-city-council is not selected. No existing feed slug corresponds to a 'Citizen Advisory Committee': addison-tx-comprehensive-plan-advisory-committee, addison-tx-town-meetings, addison-tx-public-briefings and the other feeds cannot be assigned by topic, shared members, venue or label similarity under the identity and joints rules, and no supplied evidence connects this committee to those bodies or programs. Under the sparse policy, a proven real body without an existing feed is unconfigured rather than non-city, so the action is unconfigured_body with an empty feed list and the body named above."
